            <ArticleTitle>Frontal Tendon Lengthening Plasty for Treatment of Structural Patella Baja.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e1395-e1400</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.eats.2016.08.004</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patella baja is a severe complication seen after trauma, prolonged immobilization and surgery. Several surgical methods have been described to proximalize the patella without a change in the patella tendon length. Yet, patella tendon shortening and thickening can be regarded as the hallmark pathology. As such, we describe a technique for the lengthening of the patellar tendon to pathoconformly address underlying patella baja. The technique is reproducible and gives the possibility of an early postoperative mobilization to prevent re-baja-a typical complication after patella baja surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
